Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T16:59:32.8220150Z   COMMENT_BODY: # Step 2: Prepare to collaborate
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	Your simple school website has become quite popular! After showing it at the last staff meeting, Ms. Rodriguez from the Art Club and Mr. Chen from the Chess Club came up to you super excited. They have tons of ideas for new features!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	- Ms. Rodriguez wants to add a photo gallery
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	- Mr. Chen dreams of adding a tournament bracket system for the chess/sports activities! 🎨♟️
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	While you're thrilled about their enthusiasm, you realize you need to set up some guidelines before letting them start changing code. The last thing you want is conflicting changes breaking the registration system right before spring break!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	Opening your project to other teachers at Mergington High means thinking about how everyone will collaborate together without breaking each other's code.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	**Collaborators** are the people you have granted write access to the project through repository settings.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	- Provide other people permissions to change project files while still protecting repository settings.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	- Personal repositories have simple permissions. Organization repositories allow flexible permissions such as read, write, maintain, and admin.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	To help with collaboration, GitHub provides two special files:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. **`CONTRIBUTING.md` file** - A "How to Help" guide. Some example content:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - How to prepare a developer setup of the extra-curricular activities website.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - The process for suggesting changes.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - The project's coding style preference, to keep things consistent.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - How to ask for help when stuck.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. **`CODEOWNERS` file** - Assign specific people or teams responsible for a portion of the project.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - When someone creates a pull request, GitHub will automatically ask the right person to review it.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	## ⌨️ Activity: Create a welcoming contribution guide
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	The IT Club meeting is tomorrow, and you need to prepare for Ms. Rodriguez and Mr. Chen to join the project. Let's start a document to help them contribute effectively.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. At the top navigation, return to the **Code** tab. Ensure you are on the `prepare-to-collaborate` branch.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   <img width="350" alt="image showing the correct branch" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/68cd1e7a-1b34-47eb-9f0b-095d47442b12" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the top directory, create a new file called `CONTRIBUTING.md` (case sensitive).
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Add a welcoming message.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```md
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # Contributing to the Mergington High Extra-Curricular Activities Website
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   Thank you for your interest in helping improve our school's website!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   Whether you want to add your club's activities, fix a bug, or suggest
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   new features, this guide will help you get started. 🎉
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Add instructions to help teachers quickly start developing.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```md
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ## Development Setup
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   1. Clone the repository to your computer.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   2. Install Python requirements: `pip install -r requirements.txt`.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   3. Run the development server: `python src/app.py`.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   4. Visit http://localhost:8000 in your browser to see the website.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ## Making Changes
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   1. Create a new branch for your changes.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	      - Use descriptive names like `art-gallery-feature` or `fix-chess-signup`
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   2. Make your changes and test them locally with sample student data.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	      - Use the MongoDB extension to preview the included sample date.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   3. Push your branch and create a pull request.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   4. Wait for review and address any feedback.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ## Code Style
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Follow PEP 8 for Python code (backend).
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Use clear, descriptive variable names (student_name, start_time, etc.)
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Add comments to describe blocks of logic.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Add a section for getting help.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```md
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ## Need help or have ideas?
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Check the open issues first.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	     - If your problem is there, add a comment or up-vote.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	     - If not there, create a new issue. Be as descriptive as possible.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Ask in our weekly IT Club office hours (Thursdays at lunch in Room 203).
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - For other general problems, email the tech team at [email redacted]
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the top right, use the **Commit changes...** button and commit your changes directly to `prepare-to-collaborate` branch.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	## ⌨️ Activity: Assign code ownership
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	With others joining the fun, you want to stay involved on anything affecting architecture and core functionality. Let's assign you to the related files.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. At the top navigation, return to the **Code** tab. Ensure you are on the `prepare-to-collaborate` branch.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the top directory, create a new file called `CODEOWNERS` (case sensitive and no extension).
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Add the following content:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```codeowners
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # Core functionality - changes here should be rare!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   /src/app.py                   @KokoaSkr1
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   /src/backend/database.py      @KokoaSkr1
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   /src/backend/routers/auth.py  @KokoaSkr1
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # The frontend will need refactored soon to be more object oriented.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   /src/static/   @KokoaSkr1
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the top right, use the **Commit changes...** button and commit your changes directly to `prepare-to-collaborate` branch.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. With the files committed, wait a moment for Mona to check your work, provide feedback, and share the next lesson.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	## ⌨️ Activity: (Optional) Add your first collaborator
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	Ready to let your colleague start working on that photo gallery feature? Let's do it!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	> [!IMPORTANT]
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	> This step is optional because it requires another person with a GitHub account to participate.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the top navigation, select the **Settings** tab.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the left navigation, select **Collaborators**.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
